Package: mica-sudo
Version: 1.9.16p2-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1794176058
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: sudo, mica-system
Description: Mica OS privilege for login admins: sudo, ruled by micad
 A product's privilege option: Debian's sudo, and /etc/sudoers.d/mica-admins,
 which grants nothing itself but includes /run/mica/sudoers.d. micad renders
 the rule there while its switch is on (cloudAdmins: every member of the group
 mica-admins runs anything as root without a password) and removes it when
 off. The members are the login accounts mica-accounts makes admins
 (add-login --admin), the people a provisioning agent such as mica-gce-agent
 lets in with SSH keys. root and mica are no members.
